          %title
          %h2#basic_notions_of_higher_topos_theory Basic notions of higher topos theory
          %p
            We have discussed basic notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            %a{:href => "#BasicNotionsOfToposTheory"} above
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#BasicNotionsOfHomotopyTheory"}> above
            ). The combination of the two is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            which we discuss here.
          %p
            We had explained how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            may be thought of as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
            and how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            is about relaxing the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            to that of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            and
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformation"} higher gauge transformation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+homotopy"} higher homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} higher toposes
            may be thought of as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} higher categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
            whose probe are defined only up to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
          %p (…)
          %h3#LocallyPresentbableInfinityCategories
            Locally presentable
            = succeed "-Categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The analog of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyPresentableCategory"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CombinatorialModelCategory"}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrant generation
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory"}
            below) in that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
            of
            = succeed "-inclusions." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
          %p
            That this is indeed the correct
            = succeed "-analog" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
            is the statement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"} Dugger's theorem
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DuggerTheorem"}
            below).
          %p
            Hence as we pass to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+category"} localization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+large+category"} very large category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
            at the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy-theoretic
            refinement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+large+category"} very large category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PrCat"} PrCat
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
            (Def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HoCombModCat"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
            we also refer to as a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
            we also refer to as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"}> (∞,1)-colimit
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserving
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"}> cofibrantly generated model category
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
              %strong cofibrantly generated
              if there exists two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I, J \subset Mor(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              of its class of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  have small domains according to def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassOfMorphismsWithSmallDomains"}
              %li
                %p
                  the (acyclic) cofibrations of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  are precisely the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  \-relative cell complexes), def.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalCCellComplex"}
          #CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategoryLifting.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              ), then its classes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Cof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W, Fib, Cof
              of weak equivalences, fibrations and cofibrations are equivalently expressed as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+or+projective+morphisms"} injective or projective morphisms
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LiftingAndExtension"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cof
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi I
                        %mi Inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof = (I Inj) Proj
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi Fib
                        %mo =
                        %mi I
                        %mi Inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \cap Fib = I Inj
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi Cof
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mi Inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \cap Cof = (J Inj) Proj
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Fib
                        %mo =
                        %mi J
                        %mi Inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib = J Inj
                  ;
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              It is clear from the definition that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mi Inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset (I Inj) Proj
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}
              gives an inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cof
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mi Inj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Proj
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cof \subset (I Inj) Proj
                    \\,.
            %p
              For the converse inclusion, let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mi Inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in (I Inj) Proj
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmallObjectArgument"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                          %mi Cell
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                          %mi Inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \overset{\in I Cell}{\longrightarrow}\overset{I Inj}{\longrightarrow}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract+argument"} retract argument
              lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractArgument"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a retract of an
              = succeed "-relative" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cof
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof
            %p
              This proves the first statement. Together with the closure properties of prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"}
            %p
              The proof of the third and fourth item is directly analogous, just with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              replaced for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          #CombinatorialModelCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"}> combinatorial model category
                )
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategory"}
            %ol
              %li
