                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence it is sufficient to see that an injectively fibrant simplicial presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              is objectwise a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelCategoriesOfSimplicialPresheaves"}
            %p
              To check that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuillenEquivalenceInABousfLocalization"} (10)
              is actually a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenEquivalence"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+unit"} derived adjunction unit
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+counit"} derived adjunction counit
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DerivedAdjunctionUnit"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in sSet
              any simplicial set (necessarily cofibrant), the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+unit"} derived adjunction unit
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi X
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
