                    \\mathbf{X}
            %p
              to be a weak equivalence, it is now sufficient to see that the value of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+replacement"} cofibrant replacement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{\mathbf{X}}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^0
              is a weak equivalence. But by definition of the weak equivalences of simplicial presheaves these are objectwise weak equivalences.
          #CechNerveProjectionOfLocalEpimorphismIsLocalWeakEquivalence.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_14 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"}> Cech nerve
                \-projection of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+epimorphism"} local epimorphism
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+weak+equivalence"} local weak equivalence
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Coverage"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %mi f
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{Y} \overset{\phantom{A}f\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow} \mathbf{X}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\in [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+epimorphism"} local epimorphism
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalEpimorphism"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              = succeed "-projection" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CechNerve"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Qu
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(f) \overset{}{\longrightarrow} \mathbf{X}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\in [\mathcal{C}^{op}, sSet_{Qu}]_{proj,loc}
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              in the local projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              (Prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalLocalization"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "local+epimorphism#DuggerHollanderIsaksen02"}> Dugger-Hollander-Saksen 02, corollary A.3
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#gros_toposes
            Gros
            = succeed "-Toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We have established above enough
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            that it is now fairly straightforward to generalize the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+toposes"} gros toposes
            to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+toposes"} model toposes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
